## Setup

The template's generation tasks already ran these. Repeat them only on a fresh clone:

```bash
uv sync
prek install && prek install -t commit-msg && prek install -t pre-merge-commit
```

All three shims are required — `prek install` alone wires only `pre-commit`, which silently skips
the commit-message check and breaks `--no-ff` merges into `main`.

### Live debugging for an agent (optional, once per machine)

`.debugmcp.json` lets Claude Code set breakpoints, step and inspect values through the standalone
DebugMCP CLI, with no IDE involved. The server is installed per user, so the project itself never
needs Node. It needs Node 20+:

```bash
npm install --global debugmcp
claude mcp add --scope user debugmcp-cli -- debugmcp serve --stdio
```

On native Windows, use `-- cmd /c debugmcp serve --stdio`. The name is `debugmcp-cli` because the
VS Code extension takes `debugmcp`. Prefer this to `debugmcp configure`, which also installs a
skill written for the VS Code extension. The `python-debug` skill covers using it.

## Commands

```bash
ruff format . && ruff check --fix .              # format, then auto-fix
ty check                                         # types
rumdl fmt . && rumdl check .                     # markdown
uv run pytest                                    # tests
uv run python tools/check_nested_defs.py src tests tools
prek run --all-files                             # everything above, as one gate
```

{% if project_type == "cli-modern" %}## Using the CLI

```bash
uv run {{ script_name }} --help
uv run {{ script_name }} about                  # table on stdout
uv run {{ script_name }} about --output json    # one JSON object on stdout
uv run {{ script_name }} --verbose about        # global options go before the command
```

Every setting resolves **flag, then environment variable, then default**:

| Setting | Flag | Environment variable | Default |
|---|---|---|---|
| Debug logging to stderr | `--verbose` / `--no-verbose` (global) | `{{ script_name | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_VERBOSE` | off |
| Output format | `--output` / `-o` (per command) | `{{ script_name | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_OUTPUT` | `table` |

The docstring of `config.py` says how to add a setting. An invalid value from either source exits
2 with a message naming both the flag and the variable.

Shell completion is emitted rather than installed:

```bash
{{ completion_env_var }}=source_zsh {{ script_name }} > "${ZDOTDIR:-$HOME}/completions/_{{ script_name }}"
```

{% endif %}## Updating from the template

```bash
copier update --trust
```

Requires a clean tree and the `.copier-answers.yml` written at generation. Do not delete that file.
`--trust` is required because the template declares `_tasks`. They run on the first copy only, but
copier asks for the flag anyway and exits 4 without it. Run it in your own terminal, not through
an agent: it is the flag an agent's permission classifier refuses.

